### 10. Test Error - Already verified (verify same token twice)
POST {{baseUrl}}/verify
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "nfc_token": "token_test_abc123",
  "delivery_gps": {
    "lat": 40.7129,
    "lng": -74.0061
  },
  "device_info": "iPhone 14 Pro, iOS 17"
}

### 11. Test Error - Phone verification failed (wrong phone)
POST {{baseUrl}}/verify
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "nfc_token": "token_test_abc123",
  "delivery_gps": {
    "lat": 40.8000,
    "lng": -74.1000
  },
  "device_info": "iPhone 14 Pro, iOS 17",
  "phone_last4": "9999"
}

### 12. Test GPS distance 100-300m (near verdict)
POST {{baseUrl}}/verify
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "nfc_token": "token_test_abc123",
  "delivery_gps": {
    "lat": 40.7135,
    "lng": -74.0070
  },
  "device_info": "iPhone 14 Pro, iOS 17",
  "phone_last4": "1234"
}

### 13. Test GPS distance > 300m (flagged verdict)
POST {{baseUrl}}/verify
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "nfc_token": "token_test_abc123",
  "delivery_gps": {
    "lat": 41.0000,
    "lng": -74.5000
  },
  "device_info": "iPhone 14 Pro, iOS 17",
  "phone_last4": "1234"
}

### 14. Test Error - Invalid proof_id
GET {{baseUrl}}/retrieve/invalid_proof_id_12345

###
### Instructions:
### 1. To test on local server, change @baseUrl to: @baseUrl = http://localhost:8000
### 2. To test on production server, use: @baseUrl = http://193.57.137.90:8000
### 3. Run tests in order: Enroll → Verify → Retrieve
### 4. Copy proof_id from enroll response and use it in retrieve test
### 5. Each test token can only be verified once
###
